sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant O as Owner
    participant N as Nodes on the path
    participant R as Replicas (k closest to the DID)
    Note over O: record = version 0 = algorithm | signature | DID Document<br/>key = the SHA-256 of version 0 in hashed form, the DID's suffix
    O->>N: FIND_NODE(key), iterative, alpha at a time
    N-->>O: closer nodes
    Note over O: no copy is read first, the k closest are the replicas
    par to each replica
        O->>R: STORE(key, record)
        Note over R: empty, so it checks the network first<br/>(see the STORE check diagram)
        R-->>O: Stored, or a refusal
    end
    opt a replica refused (Conflict, Stale, NewerClaimed)
        O->>R: FIND_VALUE(key) to each replica that refused, at once
        R-->>O: its record, or nothing
        Note over O: checked against version 0, then its signature<br/>version 0 signed again: ExistingRecord<br/>version 1 under the committed key: NewerVersion<br/>anything else: a replica that did not store
    end
    Note over O: Complete if every replica stored it,<br/>Degraded if some did not, or refused without showing why
